    "id": "rates-routine-r5-4-q",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The concentration $C$ mg/L of a drug in the bloodstream, $t$ hours after it is injected, is modelled by $C=50e^{-0.2t}$.\n\nFind the rate of change of the concentration after 3 hours, to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-5.49$ mg/L per hour.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C'(3)&=-0.2C(3)\\\\&=-0.2\\times50e^{-0.2\\times3}\\\\&=-10e^{-0.6}\\\\&\\approx-5.49\\text{ mg/L per hour}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
